		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2833&amp;p=31467#p31467"><![CDATA[
not really. I got distracted with building DMR repeaters. <br>I had everything correct, but I could not solder the wire to the STM pin properly as you need a very thin wire , and I shorted 2 pins so the serial port no longer works.<br>I have a microscope , and could probably fix it , but I no longer have the time. The tricky part was finding a GPS antenna to fit at the top of the radio between the knobs. I used one out of a dead GPS watch because i could not find a similar one for sale. If you install the GPS , just power it permanently with the CPU power as the GPS off feature is not very useful and the power savings is minimal.<br><br>Goos luck.<br>Luca<br>VE2WKR//W0<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1214">ve2wkr</a> — Wed May 29, 2024 2:57 am</p><hr />
